# Vendored source: ai-toolbox-cockpit catalog

These two files are vendored verbatim (byte-for-byte, no reformatting) from
kyuz0's `ai-toolbox-cockpit` project. brainrouter does not fork the schema —
it treats these as an upstream data feed and validates them structurally at
build/CI time via `scripts/sync-toolbox-catalog.sh` and
`src/toolbox_catalog/schema_validate.rs`.

- Upstream repo: https://github.com/kyuz0/ai-toolbox-cockpit
- Pinned commit: `3a4032162640d1dd9096b86bcc2b79af232eaaae`
- Commit date: 2026-09-19T15:35:37Z
- Vendored files:
  - `ai_toolbox_cockpit/assets/models.json`  -> `models.json`
  - `ai_toolbox_cockpit/assets/toolboxes.json` -> `toolboxes.json`
- Upstream schema reference (not vendored, for validator parity checks only):
  `ai_toolbox_cockpit/catalog/schema.py` (schema_version 3 as of the pinned commit)
- Fetched: see `scripts/sync-toolbox-catalog.sh` git history / CI run for the
  exact fetch date each time this pin is bumped.

## Updating the pin

Run `scripts/sync-toolbox-catalog.sh` (see that script for flags). It clones
upstream at `HEAD`, structurally validates both files with the Rust validator
(`cargo run --bin toolbox-catalog-check` / `cargo test toolbox_catalog::`),
diffs against the currently vendored copies, and — if different — updates
this file's pinned commit SHA/date and overwrites `models.json` /
`toolboxes.json`. It never auto-commits; review the diff like any other
dependency bump. The scheduled CI workflow
(`.github/workflows/sync-toolbox-catalog.yml`) runs this weekly and opens a
PR when the pin would move.

## Known backend IDs as of this pin

`llama_cpp`, `ds4`, `halogen`, `vllm`, `r9v`, `comfyui`. brainrouter's
`CatalogBackendId` (see `src/toolbox_catalog.rs`, added in PR2) parses all six
losslessly but only treats `llama_cpp`, `ds4`, `halogen`, `vllm`, `r9v` as
serving backends; `comfyui` is intentionally out of scope (image generation,
not coding-relevant — see `docs/design/ai-toolbox-cockpit-integration.md`).
Any backend id encountered outside this known set is preserved as
`CatalogBackendId::Other(String)` rather than rejected, so a new upstream
backend never breaks catalog loading.
